    "id": "guide_edu_series_part1",
    "title": "Faculty of Education: The Educator's Mindset & Academic Reality",
    "summary": "Dispelling the 'just teaching' myth, understanding the Faculty of Education structure, and mastering the foundation of academic excellence at UI.",
    "content": "Education Students Survival Guide\n\n(Beyond Just ‘Teaching’)\n\nWelcome\n\nThis book is produced by the Disciple Christian Network to help you navigate university life wisely and intentionally.\n\nIt is not theory.\n\nIt is built from real conversations with senior students who have walked this path, made mistakes, paid prices, and learned what truly works on campus.\n\nMany of them said one thing:\n\n“I wish I knew this in my first year.”\n\nThink of this book as a starter guide for your first year—your academics, your decisions, your time, and your mindset.\n\nThis book is also part of something bigger.\n\nThe FRESHERS’ AWAKENING Conference is coming—a moment created to open your eyes early, reset your mindset, and help you start school the right way.\n\nBecause the truth is simple:\n\nWhat you do in your first year matters more than you think.\n\nThrough this book and our community, we are here to help you:\n\nAvoid common freshman mistakes\n\nBuild strong academic habits early\n\nMake better decisions on campus\n\nChoose excellence over regret\n\nTo stay connected and get updates, resources, and opportunities, join our WhatsApp communities:\n\n🔹https://chat.whatsapp.com/DFoCFPS7kmQBFlxSR2vDHh\n\n🔹 https://chat.whatsapp.com/FmBJkhA6fui9CKhcmhGgip\n\n🔹 https://chat.whatsapp.com/ExJNGyUxPJu0581Nn9P8aK\n\nWelcome to school.\n\nMore importantly, welcome to doing it right.\n\n**Freshers**\n\nDear Freshers,\n\nIt is with great delight that we welcome you to this new academic journey and community of learning, growth, and discovery. Stepping into a new environment can feel both exciting and uncertain, but it is exactly within this blend of curiosity and anticipation that some of the most memorable chapters of life are written.\n\nAs freshers, you are not only joining an institution, but a family of thinkers, creators, explorers, and future leaders. This space is designed to challenge your ideas, stretch your abilities, and encourage the development of new skills and friendships. Here, you will learn to ask bold questions, embrace responsibility, and take ownership of your personal and academic progress.\n\nBeyond the lecture halls and classrooms lies a vibrant community, rich in culture, diversity, and collaboration. You will meet people from different backgrounds, discover new interests, and form connections that may last a lifetime. Do not be afraid to try new things, participate actively, and allow yourself to grow through both successes and mistakes. Every experience here, big or small, has something to teach.\n\nWe encourage you to approach these coming years with an open mind and a determined spirit. Set goals, nurture ambition, and let your curiosity lead the way. Remember that support is always within reach, your peers, mentors, and faculty are here to guide and walk alongside you.\n\n**Faculty overview**\n\nNow let me tell you all you need to know about our wonderful Faculty. The Faculty of Education is fondly referred to as “The Mother of All Faculties.” Why? Because it houses the largest number of departments in the entire university. But beyond numbers, there is a deeper meaning: education is the foundation upon which every other profession stands.\n\nIt is a great honor to be an Educator. We are the nation builders,  the shapers of minds, skills, and character. Every successful individual you know today passed through a teacher at one point or another. Schools, societies, and even nations cannot thrive without educators. Teaching is called the mother of all professions because it produces every other profession.\n\nThe Faculty of Education produces educators who go on to teach, manage, counsel, inform, research, and contribute meaningfully in various sectors. Teaching is at the core, but the possibilities are wide.\n\nThe Faculty consists of 10 departments, and they are:",
